  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 150 PM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nConfidence continues to increase for freezing temperatures\nSaturday morning. A Freeze Watch has been issues for areas that\nhave at least a 50% chances for temperatures 32 degrees or below.\nTemperatures may be as low as the mid 20s in the OK Panhandle and\nnorthern TX Panhandle. Winds will become much lighter on Saturday\nwith the arrival of our upper level high.\n\nHighs Saturday onward will steadily increase and we approach the\nnew week. 80 degree temperatures are currently expected to return\nby the midweek. Low temperatures should be the coldest on Saturday\nas well, and lows will eventually recover back into the 50s next\nweek. We are watching the development of a new upper level system\nthat could impact us by Wednesday and Thursday next week. PoPs\nreturn for that time frame, but changes are still expected as more\ndetails about the incoming system are realized.\n\nRangel",
